# Copy to .env.local. Not secret — this is a public, browser-visible value
# (Next.js exposes NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables to client code by design).
#
# 127.0.0.1, not localhost: confirmed live that on a machine with WSL2/Docker
# Desktop installed, "localhost" can resolve to ::1 first, and Windows
# silently forwards that to whatever's listening on that port inside WSL —
# not this backend, which only binds 127.0.0.1. That produced a CORS/network
# error in the browser with no useful detail (every request silently went to
# the wrong process). Pinning to 127.0.0.1 removes the ambiguity.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
